{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GEGhiWWuoDF9vnf3twfFbz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→-- Create educational_content table to store dynamic educational content\n     2→-- Categories: rules, formats, general_info, videos\n     3→\n     4→-- Create enum type for content categories\n     5→create type public.educational_content_category as enum ('rules', 'formats', 'general_info', 'videos');\n     6→\n     7→create table if not exists public.educational_content (\n     8→  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,\n     9→  title_es text not null,\n    10→  title_en text not null,\n    11→  content_es text not null,\n    12→  content_en text not null,\n    13→  category public.educational_content_category not null,\n    14→  video_url text,\n    15→  sort_order integer not null default 0,\n    16→  created_at timestamptz default now() not null\n    17→);\n    18→\n    19→-- Create index on category for efficient filtering\n    20→create index educational_content_category_idx on public.educational_content (category);\n    21→\n    22→-- Create index on sort_order for efficient ordering\n    23→create index educational_content_sort_order_idx on public.educational_content (sort_order);\n    24→\n    25→-- Enable Row Level Security\n    26→alter table public.educational_content enable row level security;\n    27→\n    28→-- RLS policy: public read access\n    29→create policy \"Anyone can read educational content\"\n    30→  on public.educational_content for select\n    31→  using (true);\n    32→\n    33→-- RLS policy: admin write operations\n    34→-- Note: service_role bypasses RLS entirely, so these policies apply to authenticated users only\n    35→-- For now, no authenticated users can write - all write operations go through service_role (server-side)\n    36→-- When an admin role system is implemented, update these policies to check admin status\n    37→create policy \"Admin can insert educational content\"\n    38→  on public.educational_content for insert\n    39→  with check (false);\n    40→\n    41→create policy \"Admin can update educational content\"\n    42→  on public.educational_content for update\n    43→  using (false);\n    44→\n    45→create policy \"Admin can delete educational content\"\n    46→  on public.educational_content for delete\n    47→  using (false);\n    48→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GqDev2JtXswRxec2ndCFcz","session_id":"390ca8d4-cf33-40e5-867b-fd8aefb9a312","uuid":"854b3924-b6e6-428d-b6c1-a84e40268f49"}
